# Vayu — npm settings.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS: without it, `npm install` and `npm ci` both fail on a
# fresh clone. Not slowly, not with a warning — they refuse to resolve at all:
#
#   Could not resolve dependency:
#   peerOptional @sveltejs/kit@"^2.0.0" from better-auth@1.6.28
#   Found: @sveltejs/kit@3.0.0-next.23
#
# better-auth declares an OPTIONAL peer on SvelteKit 2, and this project is on
# the SvelteKit 3 pre-release (adapter-cloudflare 8 requires it). npm 7+ treats
# an unsatisfiable peer as fatal even when it is optional, so the install stops
# on a dependency better-auth does not actually need from us — nothing here
# imports its SvelteKit integration; the app uses better-auth's framework-
# agnostic core from services/auth/better-auth.js.
#
# The node_modules tree this repo has been developed against was clearly built
# by passing --legacy-peer-deps on the command line and never writing it down,
# which is why the failure was invisible to everyone who already had one and
# total for anyone who did not. This records the decision instead of leaving it
# in somebody's shell history.
#
# Drop this line when better-auth widens that peer range to include SvelteKit
# 3, or when it is no longer a dependency.
legacy-peer-deps=true
